        <h2>2. Acceptance of These Terms</h2>
        <p>By accessing this website or enrolling in the mentorship program, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, please do not use our Services.</p>

        <h2>3. Description of Services</h2>
        <p>We provide live, small-group Japanese language mentorship sessions, JLPT-focused practice, a personalized study roadmap, and access to a custom kanji and vocabulary app with spaced repetition, delivered on a recurring 4-week cycle.</p>

        <h2>4. Enrollment and Payment</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Enrollment is completed by selecting a subscription plan and paying through our secure checkout page, operated by our payment processor, Stripe. At checkout, you will be asked to expressly accept these Terms before completing payment.</li>
          <li>The mentorship program is billed on a recurring 4-week cycle that renews automatically until cancelled. Three subscription plans are available, depending on the language of instruction and your location:
            <ul>
              <li>440 RON, billed every 4 weeks, for sessions delivered in Romanian;</li>
              <li>119 USD, billed every 4 weeks, for sessions delivered in English;</li>
              <li>119 EUR, billed every 4 weeks, for students located within the European Union.</li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>These prices do not include VAT, as Kitsunebi Miyabi SRL is not a VAT payer ("neplătitoare de TVA") under Romanian law. Pricing is subject to change with reasonable notice for future billing cycles.</li>
          <li>Payment is processed securely by Stripe. We do not collect or store your full card details; see our <a href="/privacy-policy" class="highlight">Privacy Policy</a> for details on how payment data is handled.</li>
          <li>By completing a subscription purchase, you authorize us to charge your chosen payment method every 4 weeks until you cancel in accordance with Section 5. You will receive an invoice by email after each successful payment.</li>
          <li>Access to live sessions and the vocab app for a given cycle is conditional on payment for that cycle being received.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Cancellation and Right of Withdrawal</h2>
        <p>You may cancel your subscription at any time by contacting us at <strong class="highlight text-red-300">vici.sensei@gmail.com</strong>. Cancelling stops future renewals only: you retain full access to live sessions and the vocab app for the remainder of the 4-week cycle you have already paid for, and your payment method will not be charged again after that. Cancellation does not entitle you to a refund for the current cycle or any previous cycle, whether or not you attended all scheduled sessions.</p>
        <p>If you are a consumer entering into this contract at a distance, Romanian law (GEO no. 34/2014) grants you the right to withdraw from the contract within 14 calendar days without giving any reason. By checking the box to accept these Terms and completing payment on our checkout page before this 14-day period has elapsed, you expressly request that we begin performing the Services immediately, and you acknowledge and agree that you lose the right of withdrawal once the corresponding live session(s) have been fully delivered, in accordance with the exceptions provided by that law.</p>
        <p>You may exercise your right of withdrawal, where it still applies, by contacting us at <strong class="highlight text-red-300">vici.sensei@gmail.com</strong>.</p>

        <h2>6. Your Responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate contact and billing information;</li>
          <li>Attend your scheduled weekly live session at its fixed time. Because sessions are delivered in a small-group format shared with other students, missed sessions cannot be rescheduled or made up, and no refund or credit is given for a session you did not attend;</li>
          <li>Ensure you have the equipment and internet connection necessary to join live sessions on the platform used to host them;</li>
          <li>Use the kanji and vocabulary app for your own personal, non-commercial study only;</li>
          <li>Not disclose to anyone outside your group any personal information you learn about other participants during group sessions.</li>
        </ul>

